      "hints": [
        "Divide $p(x)$ by the known quadratic factor $x^2-x+2$, beginning with the leading term $4x^2$ in the quotient.",
        "Continue the division until the remainder is expressed in terms of $a$ and $b$.",
        "Because divisibility requires the entire linear remainder to vanish, equate both its coefficients to zero.",
        "Solve the resulting simultaneous conditions for $a$ and $b$."
      ],
